   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the county of Saratoga to discontinue for reforestation purposes the use of certain lands and to convey such lands",
    "basePrintNo": "S6905",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6905-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Saratoga County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6905\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act authorizing the county of Saratoga to discontinue for reforesta-\ntion purposes the use of certain lands and to convey such lands\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 of the bill authorizes the County of Saratoga to discontinue\nthe use of land for reforestation purposes that is identified in section\n2 and to convey the same to the Town of Moreau in exchange for a new\nparcel identified in section 3 that shall be dedicated for reforestation\npurposes.\n\nSection 2 provides a legal description of the property to be conveyed.\n\nSection 3 provides a legal description of the property to be acquired by\nthe County in exchange that shall be dedicated for reforestation\npurposes.\n\nSection 4 provides the bill shall be effective immediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe County of Saratoga is willing to assist the Town of Moreau in regard\nto a proposed water pump station by conveying a .082 acre parcel to the\nTown.\n\nHowever, the parcel in question has been dedicated for reforestation\npurposes and by virtue of Section 219 of the County Law, an act of the\nState Legislature is necessary in order to transfer the land.\n\nThe County as part of the agreement will replace the loss of reforesta-\ntion land by obtaining from the Town another parcel of equal or greater\nfair market value to the lands being alienated which the County will\ndedicate for reforestation purposes.\n\nThe new parcel is already owned by the County, and is suitable for\nreforestation purposes.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the State or to the County of Saratoga.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
